{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1086042-some-more-beast-questions","id":1086042,"title":"Some more Beast Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-30T20:54:46-07:00","id":1086042,"title":"Some more Beast Questions","content":"Oh this book... Ok here are a few questions.<br /> 1. When one becomes a beast, when they are consumed, does that person dies and the beast takes on their persona, or do the two merge? Does the Beast self ever emerge in the real world? <br /> 2. Does the beast find you because you have something like the beast in your heart or could it be pure chance? <br /> 3.When feeding are you taking the person into your lair while they dream and then feeding on then while they are afraid? <br /> 4.Do you have no morality but just Satiety? Does feeding a little at a time make you &quot;good&quot; while eating all at once makes you bad?<br /> 5. Is the Primordial Dream the Skien of Changeling? Can Changelings and Beast run into each other in the Dream World?<br /> 6. I have ideas, but would love some ideas for this Beast <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/516858494725226301/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/516858494725226301/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/516858494725226301/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.pinterest.com/pin/516858494725226301/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:12:08-07:00","id":1086047,"title":"","content":"1. Those aren't objective questions. What is the &quot;self&quot;? If it's the mind that says &quot;I am&quot; and is self aware, then no the person just merges with their Horror. If it's the Fire of the human soul, then yes that's fully consumed and replaced.<br /> <br /> Horrors can physically manifest via Primordial Pathways. Call down your Lair.<br /> <br /> There are also various &quot;character conclusion&quot; routes that can allow becoming physically your Horror discussed in the Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:17:51-07:00","id":1086053,"title":"","content":"4. &quot;Morality&quot; isn't a stat for anyone in a second edition Chronicles of Darkness. Mortals of mental Integrity. Vampire &quot;Humanity&quot; is a measure of alienation not moral goodness. Mage &quot;Wisdom&quot; is about control and prudence with magic, not morality (you can have a very good person with very low Wisdom because they're reckless). Werewolves want to keep Harmony balanced, a high rating is as bad as a low one, etc etc.<br /> <br /> Moral goodness does not need a stat to determine whether or not it applies to the character. Morality is more abstract than that.. Satiety does not make you good or bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:19:16-07:00","id":1086055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1086042-some-more-beast-questions#post1086042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. When one becomes a beast, when they are consumed, does that person dies and the beast takes on their persona, or do the two merge?</div> </div> </div> </div>You remain the same person, but you now have a piece of potent predatory iconography where most people keep their soul.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the Beast self ever emerge in the real world? </div> </div> </div>Only literally if things go very wrong. Atavisms manifest the effects of your Horror's physiology in ways that are less overt.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Does the beast find you because you have something like the beast in your heart or could it be pure chance? </div> </div> </div>The former. &quot;Pure chance&quot; is seldom actually a random pull where the supernatural is concerned.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3.When feeding are you taking the person into your lair while they dream and then feeding on then while they are afraid? </div> </div> </div>Nope. If you're Starving and your Horror feeds itself deeply enough to drag someone's dreaming self back to the Lair then you stand to get a major meal, but normal feeding is just doing things that echo the Horror's Hunger in the waking world, possibly while bodily bringing a target into the Lair for a time.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4.Do you have no morality but just Satiety? </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does feeding a little at a time make you &quot;good&quot; while eating all at once makes you bad? </div> </div> </div>Big meals tend to mean your Satiety rating goes up and down more frequently and consistent high Satiety tends to mean you minimize the intensity of your impact on the world, often through taking a lot of little bites instead of a few huge ones.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Is the Primordial Dream the Skien of Changeling? </div> </div> </div>No.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Changelings and Beast run into each other in the Dream World? </div> </div> </div>Yup, as can anyone else who's in a dream that a Beast or their Horror is visiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:20:13-07:00","id":1086056,"title":"","content":"5. No the Primordial Dream is further in the Temenos. It's what's on the other side of the Omphalos Stone, which marks the boundary between it and the archetypes of human civilization.<br /> <br /> That said, we don't know how deep Changelings can go in Second Edition yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T20:23:09-07:00","id":1086445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1086042-some-more-beast-questions#post1086042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh this book... Ok here are a few questions.<br /> 1. When one becomes a beast, when they are consumed, does that person dies and the beast takes on their persona, or do the two merge? Does the Beast self ever emerge in the real world?<br /> 2. Does the beast find you because you have something like the beast in your heart or could it be pure chance?<br /> 3.When feeding are you taking the person into your lair while they dream and then feeding on then while they are afraid?<br /> 4.Do you have no morality but just Satiety? Does feeding a little at a time make you &quot;good&quot; while eating all at once makes you bad?<br /> 5. Is the Primordial Dream the Skien of Changeling? Can Changelings and Beast run into each other in the Dream World?<br /> 6. I have ideas, but would love some ideas for this Beast<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/516858494725226301/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/516858494725226301/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/516858494725226301/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.pinterest.com/pin/516858494725226301/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To answer question 1, you retain your human memories and are capable of passing yourself off as human in public, but your soul has merged with the horror. You may be capable of imitating human behavior and thought processes, but on the inside, you're a monster who feeds on the suffering of others. Whether you use your humanity as a tool to blend in with society, or cast it aside is up to you. But throwing caution to the wind often attracts Heroes, as well as other disgruntled relatives who think you need to have a forced intervention.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To answer question 2, the book is intentionally vague about this topic and gives conflicting accounts on how it works. One account says that you were born a monster (much like Werewolves), but never realized your true heritage until the time of the Devouring. Another account says that the horror chooses you because you have a keen understanding of the Primordial Dream and the ability to decipher its lessons. It is ultimately up to the Story Teller to decide the true nature of how Beasts are created.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To answer question 3, Beasts feed on fear, which you can harvest just about anywhere. It is easiest to feed inside your lair, but you are also vulnerable there, since your lair is an extension of your soul. Damaging (or worse, destroying) your Lair has massive consequences. So it is safer to feed in the physical world, even though your powers are restricted there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To answer question 4, the thing that makes you good is that you try to educate people through fear. The book says <i>&quot;Eat to live, don't live to eat&quot;</i> Your horror doesn't care about anything beyond satisfying its own hunger, but your mind is at least partially human, which means you get to exercise some degree of restraint, as long as you maintain control. Any Beast who plans to live long tries to incorporate some kind of lesson beyond their feedings, so that the victims (who survive the process) come away wiser than they were before. Other Beasts simply don't give a shit and just take the quick and easy path to slaking their hunger. Consequences be damned!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To answer question 5, the Primordial Dream is the collective essence of all mankind's fears. Every nightmare you've ever had, every monster you've ever imagined, everything that has ever made you feel scared; that's what the Primordial Dream is. Beasts are also very, very skilled at traveling between other worlds. They've essentially got a skeleton key to the Chronicles of Darkness multiverse; so yes, it is possible for the two to meet up with each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And to answer question number 6, wait - that's not a question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-25-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T22:22:50-07:00","id":1086477,"title":"","content":"@Nyrufa,<br /> <br /> I think you might be mixing up the Beast Incarnate for a regular Beast. <br /> <br /> The Devouring doesn't take away a person's humanity. It fuses it with the needs of a Horror, and all the benefits and problems that entails. You retain your memories, human emotions, human urges, and human bodily needs. You also gain the endless hunger of the Horror, the Horror's powers, and the responsibility of feeding the Horror as well as the consiquences for what happens when you don't. That's the core essence of a Begotten's Legend and Life. The Legend is all that the Horror is, wants, and represents, and the Life is all that you personally hold onto that makes you still human and a person.<br /> <br /> The Beast Incarnate on the other had is a perfect fusion of person and predator. It's so far removed from human needs and urges (and the Horror's needs and urges too) that it might as well be a completely different entity cometely removed from Beast the Primordial if it wasn't for it's connection to the Primordial Dream. It can use both it's human and Begotten memories to pretent to be either well enough, but is unquestionably a monstrous other with near immortality and no worry about hunger or predation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:23:05-07:00","id":1086973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1086042-some-more-beast-questions?p=1086477#post1086477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Nyrufa,<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast Incarnate on the other had is a perfect fusion of person and predator. It's so far removed from human needs and urges (and the Horror's needs and urges too) that it might as well be a completely different entity cometely removed from Beast the Primordial if it wasn't for it's connection to the Primordial Dream. It can use both it's human and Begotten memories to pretent to be either well enough, but is unquestionably a monstrous other with near immortality and no worry about hunger or predation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, the Beast Incarnate becomes one with their Legend, the don't simply act it out, they fully embody it. The invincible enemy, the untrackable killer, the mind shattering abomination, est. They have access to powers and traits that only exist in the most grandiose mythologies, such as the power to turn people to stone with a gaze. Basically a Gorgon Incarnate would be able to one shot anybody stupid enough to pick a fight with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:40:18-07:00","id":1095438,"title":"","content":"Hey guys. Not sure if this is the best place for this but I wanted to ask everyone's opinion about a rules decision we made during a game over the weekend. To make a long story short an ally (but not brood mate) was fighting an Insatiable in his Lair. My horror and his are quite similar with many of the same Lair traits and I entered his lair to assist him. He made me immune to his tilts but, as I was in my human form, I was severely limited from helping.<br /> <br /> Looking into the primordial pathway rules it did not seem like there was any particular rule against opening pathways between beasts Lairs so the storyteller ruled I could roll to do so and upon succeeding my horror came to join with me and I battled alongside him in his lair. Going forwards this will no doubt bring us closer and maybe bring him into the brood properly. <br /> <br /> But in the short-term I wanted to ask everyone's opinion of this decision? Does this action fit with your understanding of pathways and Lairs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T12:07:08-07:00","id":1095586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1086042-some-more-beast-questions?p=1095438#post1095438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys. Not sure if this is the best place for this but I wanted to ask everyone's opinion about a rules decision we made during a game over the weekend. To make a long story short an ally (but not brood mate) was fighting an Insatiable in his Lair. My horror and his are quite similar with many of the same Lair traits and I entered his lair to assist him. He made me immune to his tilts but, as I was in my human form, I was severely limited from helping.<br /> <br /> Looking into the primordial pathway rules it did not seem like there was any particular rule against opening pathways between beasts Lairs so the storyteller ruled I could roll to do so and upon succeeding my horror came to join with me and I battled alongside him in his lair. Going forwards this will no doubt bring us closer and maybe bring him into the brood properly.<br /> <br /> But in the short-term I wanted to ask everyone's opinion of this decision? Does this action fit with your understanding of pathways and Lairs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the Dream's the easiest place to open Pathways to? Seems perfectly within spec.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}